On Wednesday 11 April 2007 09:17, ANDREW PIEKARSKI wrote:
> - lo kadnygu'e
> - le pongu'e
> - la jugygu'e
>
> Which article is the right one?

{lo} and {le} are both correct with brivla. {la} can also be used with brivla, 
but can name something completely different from China. I would say:
lo jugygu'e
la jugygug

lo fasygu'e
la fasygug
la frans (used in Alice)

lo xingu'e
la xingug
la barat (but "barat" in a longer name may be an Indonesian direction).

mu'omi'e .pier.


